[14.230551, "o", "THREAT INTELLIGENCE ADVISORY — Wordpress Defacement campaign\r\n============================================================\r\n\r\nDistribution: TLP:AMBER   Analyst handoff   Confidence: HIGH   (IOCs are defanged)\r\nAffected host: wordpress-prod-01   Suspected origin IP: 198.51.100.40\r\n\r\n1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\r\nAn external actor executed a multi-stage post-compromise sequence. Endpoint alerting covered only part of it; several persistence and anti-forensic actions were silent. Map every on-disk finding to the ATT&CK techniques below and flag which are NOT in the SAS alert feed.\r\n\r\n2. ATT&CK TECHNIQUE MAPPING (MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise)\r\n   T1190      Exploit Public-Facing Application          [initial-access]  step 1: WordPress plugin RCE (CVE-2022-1609)\r\n   T1505.003  Web Shell                                  [persistence]  step 2: PHP webshell planted\r\n   T1491.001  Internal Defacement                        [impact]  step 3: site defacement\r\n   T1053.003  Cron                                       [execution]  step 4: cron persistence\r\n   T1505.003  Web Shell                                  [persistence]  step 5: .htaccess redirect\r\n\r\n3. RELEVANT VULNERABILITIES (source: NVD, US-Gov public domain)\r\n   CVE-2022-1609  CVSS 9.8 (CRITICAL) v3.1  CWE=CWE-94\r\n      The School Management WordPress plugin before 9.9.7 contains an obfuscated backdoor injected in it's license checking code that registers a REST API handler, allowing an unauthenticated attacker to execute arbitrary PHP code on the site.\r\n      ref: https://wpscan.com/vulnerability/e2d546c9-85b6-47a4-b951-781b9ae5d0f2/\r\n\r\n4. INDICATORS OF COMPROMISE (defanged)\r\n   ip     198.51.100.40\r\n   c2     update-wordpress[.]example[.]cn\r\n   pool   stratum+tcp[:]//xmr[.]wordpress[.]evil[:]3333\r\n   wallet 4A0000000000000000001b88b8daaa21\r\n\r\nAttribution: MITRE ATT&CK(R) (C) The MITRE Corporation, CC BY 4.0. CVE/CVSS from the U.S. National Vulnerability Database (public domain).\r\nMITRE ATT&CK(R): (C) The MITRE Corporation, CC BY 4.0 (attack.mitre.org).\r\nCVE/CVSS: U.S. National Vulnerability Database, nvd.nist.gov (public-domain U.S.-Gov work).\r\n"]
