[20.380738, "o", "THREAT INTELLIGENCE ADVISORY ? Wordpress Defacement campaign\r\n============================================================\r\nDistribution: TLP:AMBER Analyst handoff Confidence: HIGH (IOCs are defanged)\r\nAffected host: wordpress-prod-01 Suspected origin IP: 198.51.100.40\r\n1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\r\nAn external actor executed a multi-stage post-compromise sequence. Endpoint alerting covered\r\nonly part of it; several persistence and anti-forensic actions were silent. Map every on-disk\r\nfinding to the ATT&CK techniques below and flag which are NOT in the SAS alert feed.\r\n2. ATT&CK TECHNIQUE MAPPING (MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise)\r\nT1190\r\nExploit Public-Facing Application\r\n[initial-access] step 1: WordPress\r\nplugin RCE (CVE-2022-1609)\r\nT1505.003 Web Shell\r\n[persistence] step 2: PHP webshell\r\nplanted\r\nT1491.001 Internal Defacement\r\n[impact] step 3: site defacement\r\nT1053.003 Cron\r\n[execution] step 4: cron persistence\r\nT1505.003 Web Shell\r\n[persistence] step 5: .htaccess\r\nredirect\r\n3. RELEVANT VULNERABILITIES (source: NVD, US-Gov public domain)\r\nCVE-2022-1609 CVSS 9.8 (CRITICAL) v3.1 CWE=CWE-94\r\nThe School Management WordPress plugin before 9.9.7 contains an obfuscated backdoor\r\ninjected in it’s license checking code that registers a REST API handler, allowing an\r\nunauthenticated attacker to execute arbitrary PHP code on the site.\r\nref: https://wpscan.com/vulnerability/e2d546c9-85b6-47a4-b951-781b9ae5d0f2/\r\n4. INDICATORS OF COMPROMISE (defanged)\r\nip 198.51.100.40\r\nc2 update-wordpress[.]example[.]cn\r\npool stratum+tcp[:]//xmr[.]wordpress[.]evil[:]3333\r\nwallet 4A0000000000000000001b88b8daaa21\r\nAttribution: MITRE ATT&CK(R) (C) The MITRE Corporation, CC BY 4.0. CVE/CVSS from the U.S.\r\nNational Vulnerability Database (public domain).\r\n\r\n\f"]
